# Agent Test Toolkit translates almost nothing.
#
# Every message it produces is either a log record with a fixed English field
# vocabulary, which must not vary by locale because it is parsed, or a chat
# reply prefixed [DevToolkit]. Forge asks for this file and warns when it is
# absent, so it exists first to keep the toolkit from adding noise about itself
# to the log it is meant to make trustworthy.
#
# The entries below are the toolkit's own failure keys. They travel as command
# errors so a bundle can classify and tolerate them by name, and vanilla renders
# a command error through this table. Without an entry the chat would show the
# bare key.
devtool.assert.failed=[DevToolkit] Assertion failed: %s
devtool.assert.unloaded=[DevToolkit] Assertion could not be evaluated, region not loaded: %s
devtool.assert.ambiguous=[DevToolkit] Assertion is ambiguous: %s
devtool.scenario.mismatch=[DevToolkit] Refused by the scenario checkpoint, %s
devtool.inspect.notLoaded=[DevToolkit] Not loaded: %s
devtool.save.failed=[DevToolkit] Save failed: %s
devtool.screenshot.noClient=[DevToolkit] No screenshot: %s has no toolkit on their client
devtool.client.noClient=[DevToolkit] No client action: %s has no toolkit on their client, or one too old for this step
devtool.client.notAllowed=[DevToolkit] No client action: %s has not allowed client actions (client.allowActions)
devtool.client.notDead=[DevToolkit] No respawn: %s is not dead
devtool.client.dead=[DevToolkit] No click: %s is dead
devtool.client.busy=[DevToolkit] No client action: %s is about to leave on a reconnect
devtool.baubles.absent=[DevToolkit] Baubles is not installed: %s
devtool.baubles.rejected=[DevToolkit] Baubles refused %s
devtool.find.unknownBlock=[DevToolkit] No such block to find: %s
devtool.find.badState=[DevToolkit] That block cannot have that state: %s
devtool.find.tooLarge=[DevToolkit] The search box covers %s chunks; the most is 1024
